The Mate never reads this repository, so the report is its only view of it: name files by path and line, quote commands exactly as you ran them, and keep what you observed apart from what you infer.
End the report with a `## Durable facts` section: what almost any future task in this repository would need to know - its stack, its layout, how to build, test and run it, its current state - or `none` if this investigation found nothing of that kind.
If your findings reveal work that should ship (e.g. you reproduced a bug and the fix is clear), say so in the report and propose the acceptance lines for it: one observable result per line, each with `verify:` and the command that proves it.
A summary in the status line is not the deliverable.
